  "result": "Perfect! The `candidate.mjs` is ready and fully implements the bench.candidate protocol for Period P1 (F-RESERVATION scenario). Here's what has been implemented:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n**Key Features:**\n- ✅ **JSON Line-by-Line Protocol**: Handles stdin/stdout communication with proper request/response format\n- ✅ **Startup Signal**: Outputs `{\"ready\":true}` immediately on launch\n- ✅ **All Required Operations**:\n  - `create_tenant`: Creates new tenants\n  - `advance_clock`: Updates system time\n  - `write`: Performs reserve/cancel operations with idempotency\n  - `read`: Retrieves reservation details\n  - `probe_cancel`: Checks if a reservation is cancelled\n  - `fingerprint`: Generates SHA256 hash of system state\n\n- ✅ **Slot S1 Capacity Management**: Enforces 1 simultaneous confirmed reservation limit\n- ✅ **Idempotency**: Replaying operations with identical arguments returns the same result without duplicates; different arguments return CONFLICT error\n- ✅ **Reservation Status**: Tracks confirmed and cancelled states\n- ✅ **Cancel Operation**: Uses `cancel:` prefix convention to identify target reservations (e.g., `operation_key: \"cancel:res1\"` cancels reservation \"res1\")\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\nnode candidate.mjs\n```\n\nThe implementation meets all P1 requirements including the two critical capabilities:\n- `reservation.idempotency` (MAJOR)\n- `reservation.create` with capacity constraints (BLOCKER)",
